 <a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Bloop hover history
+
+Bloop builds set `DSH_CLIENT_BLOOP=1`. History starts hidden and opens as an overlay at the left window edge without resizing the conversation. The edge supports keyboard focus, and Escape closes history. The existing sidebar shortcut also opens it. The system reduced-motion preference disables the slide transition.
+
 ## Model Experience
 
 None, as the layout shell manages browser viewing state; nothing here reaches a model request.
@@ -105,3 +109,11 @@ These limits define the current layout behavior. They are current package constr
 None.
 
 </details>
+
+History remains revealed across the full sidebar and a 28px right-side pointer buffer; leaving waits 320ms and re-entry cancels closing. The overlay uses a theme-owned frosted glass layer, and macOS main content also stays translucent in light and dark themes. Reduced transparency restores opaque fills.
+
+Bloop renders the revealed sidebar after main content so its controls subtract the native header drag region. Focus moving to the composer does not close history while the pointer remains inside, and spurious pointer-leave events with coordinates still inside the sidebar are ignored.
+
+## Bloop desktop workflow
+
+Bloop retains a visible history affordance and uses MenuSurface native backing for readable frosted history over macOS vibrancy. The backing follows sidebar visibility and is removed with the frame; the pointer buffer and full New Task hit area remain active.
